Per-step draft length for the DSpark paper scheduler, on top of
vllm-apertus-dspark-paper-scheduler.patch (apply that one first). Enabled with
VLLM_DSPARK_DRAFT_CUT=1 next to VLLM_DSPARK_VERIFY_MODE=paper. Not in the
paper, which drafts every slot each step.

Under load the paper scheduler verifies ~3 of 7 drafted slots, but the draft
step still runs the full block (17 ms of a ~80 ms step at 256 requests on
GH200). Here the scheduler also picks how many slots the step drafts, D: the
draft step costs draft_ms(R, D) (profiled at engine start per length) and D
maximises the same objective, tau * SPS(B), with admission limited to the
first D slots. The drafter then runs as a k=D drafter for that step (a block
of D query tokens and D sequential Markov steps, one CUDA graph set per
length; the fixed k=3 drafter shows a shorter block keeps the acceptance of
the first slots), and the next step's GPU top-K picks among the drafted
slots only. Survival of slots a shortened draft did not produce is
extrapolated with the running mean conditional confidence per slot.
VLLM_DSPARK_DRAFT_LENGTHS restricts the lengths (default 1..k).
